    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (64.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.78) anchor the LawDog lineup as our strongest plays. Both benefit significantly from favorable park factors and high-upside matchups against mediocre arms in Singer and McGreevy, respectively. **Masyn Winn** also presents a strong profile (61.81) due to a standout +19% SP skill advantage against Kelly, whose 5.29 xERA suggests a prime opportunity for **Masyn Winn** to manufacture runs and utilize his speed\u2014a critical factor given our league's weighting toward stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** (60.69) is a compelling start in the outfield; despite a slight negative SP skill modifier, his massive +13% dynamic platoon edge against Cavalli makes him a high-efficiency play for power production.\n\nWe face a difficult bench decision regarding **Luis Arraez** (44.52), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Luis Arraez** offers a strong baseline for batting average, the matchup against Miller\u2019s elite 2.85 xERA severely penalized his projection, forcing him to the bench in favor of hitters with higher ceiling potential against weaker opposing pitching. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh** (53.78) and **Jonathan Aranda** (47.18); while both are active, they are fighting significant negative platoon adjustments today. **Jonathan Aranda** is particularly leveraged against the lefty Rivera, and if **Cal Raleigh** continues to struggle with his current park factor deficit, we will look to rotate in **Will Smith** or **Yainer Diaz** for upcoming series to preserve our game caps. Finally, take note that **Bryce Harper** is confirmed out today, removing a high-floor asset from our available pool and necessitating the current configuration in the corner and utility spots.",
